    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n60564" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κῠδών-ιος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κυδωνία</span>) <u>Cydonian</u>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μᾶλα</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>quinces</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Stesich.
				29
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Alcm.
				143
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Canthar.
				6
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Phylarch.
				10
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				J.
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μηλίδες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ibyc.
					1.1
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κυδώνια, τά</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				1.115
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> metaph.,
				<i>swelling like a quince</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ.
				τιτθία</span>, of a young girl's breasts, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ach.</u>
				1199
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κυδώνιον: μέγα καὶ ἀξιόλογον, ἢ
				ἀπατηλόν, δόλιον, λοίδορον</span> (cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κύδος</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i></div>
